course: dictionary
lesson: 9248
title: Feeling words in stories
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words show how a character feels, not just what they do. «Sorrowfully» is one of them. Sorrow is deep sadness, often about a loss, so sorrowfully means in a very sad way.
explain: In Alice in Wonderland, the Mock Turtle sighs and sings sorrowfully about his schooldays. He is not just singing. The word tells you he feels sad when he thinks back to the past. Ask yourself: what is the character feeling, and what words around it give you a clue?
explain: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole finds his little home again and looks at it sorrowfully. The word shows he feels deep sadness, not happiness. Look at the other words in the sentence for more clues.
fact: Sorrowfully means in a very sad way, full of sorrow or grief.
fact: «Sadly» is a softer word; «sorrowfully» is more serious and deep.
fact: Sorrow often comes from a loss, such as missing a home or a time that has gone.
fact: The Mock Turtle in Alice in Wonderland sings sorrowfully about his schooldays.
fact: A good check is to swap in another word, such as mournfully. If it still fits, you have found the meaning.
exercise: The Mock Turtle sings sorrowfully about his schooldays. How does he sing? | Quickly, to finish his song | *In a very sad way, full of sorrow | In a whisper, so no one can hear | Happily and loudly
exercise: Mole looks sorrowfully at his little home. What feeling does this show? | Excitement about a party | Anger at a neighbour | *Deep sadness | Surprise at a gift
exercise: Which word means the same as sorrowfully? | Loudly | Happily | *Mournfully | Quickly
test: «His home had called him sorrowfully, reproachfully, but with no bitterness or anger.» What does sorrowfully mean here? | In a cheerful way | In a sleepy way | In an angry way, full of bitterness | *In a sad way, full of sorrow
test: In the same sentence, the home calls Mole «with no bitterness or anger». What feeling does the home show? | Joy | *Sadness, without anger | Fear | Anger
exam: Which sentence shows a character feeling deep sadness? | «She laughed loudly at the joke.» | *«He looked sorrowfully at the empty nest.» | «The sun was hot and bright.» | «They ran to the shops.»
